            <ArticleTitle>Double-stenting in distal left main lesions: Let's crush.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>24-25</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccd.26894</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Unprotected distal left main (ULM) lesions often require double-stenting. In the MITO Registry, a mini-crush stenting technique was safer than culotte stenting. Performing mini-crush arises as the best approach in patients with distal ULM lesions requiring elective double-stenting.</AbstractText>
